      "message": "fix(post): grblHAL, TinyG and Carvera state the clearance Z before the first X/Y traverse\n\nAfter a tool change (and at the program's start) the three posts wrote a\nbare X/Y rapid at whatever height the change left the tip - the #1614\nhazard: a long tool on a high work offset can stand below the part top\nthere. Each now writes a Z-only G0 to the section's ClearancePlane, else\nits RetractPlane (never below the move's own Z) before that traverse, as\ntormach.cps does in PR #1618. A stream that states neither plane is\nrefused by name with #1618's wording. A feed's rapid down to its start\nheight is skipped when the traverse already stated that height.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance.rs. Goldens gain the\none G0 Z line each; test streams that stated no plane now state one, as\npost::dump does. The Fanuc family (fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm,\nsinumerik, heidenhain) remains for a second PR.\n\nRefs #1616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
