      "message": "fix(post): Carvera keeps X/Y first after M6, then states the clearance Z\n\nReview notes from M3 on 49ec197f:\n\n- Carvera, option (c). Right after M6 T.. the Carvera traverses X/Y\n  first, at the changer's exit height (main's order), then\n  G0 Z<ClearancePlane|RetractPlane> (never below the move's Z), then the\n  descent. Nothing we have read says where the firmware parks X/Y after a\n  tool change, and a Z-only rapid down at the rack's X/Y could meet the\n  stored tools when the stock is thin. A program start with no tool change\n  still states Z first. grblHAL and TinyG are unchanged.\n- The stale \"X/Y first at the safe/changer height\" comments in\n  carvera.cps, grblhal.cps and tinyg.cps now match the code.\n- The decision file records option (c) with the options considered, and\n  says this PR closes #1616 for these posts; the Fanuc-family half is #1633.\n\nPinned by first_traverse_clearance (Carvera order after M6, Z first at a\nprogram start with no tool change). The Carvera goldens move again: the\nadded G0 Z now follows the X/Y line after M6.\n\nFixes #1616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
